gnome-shell-extension-zark (1.1-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * GNOME Shell 51 (Ubuntu 26.10) as well as 50 (Ubuntu 26.04): the menu
    closes without animating before the details dialog opens, as on 50.
  * With /proc mounted hidepid, where root's processes cannot be seen, a
    run's missing pid no longer makes it orphaned: its heartbeat says
    running or stalled (orphan rule 4 of the status contract, as zark
    2.2 amends it; rules 3 and 5 unchanged).

 -- Juanmi Taboada <juanmi@juanmitaboada.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 12:58:00 +0100

gnome-shell-extension-zark (1.0-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * First release: the panel indicator and its menu, the details dialog
    (pools, datasets, backup drives and their points by month),
    notifications and preferences, read from the status files of zark 2.1.

 -- Juanmi Taboada <juanmi@juanmitaboada.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:05:00 +0100
